# Golden fixtures are compared byte-for-byte against rendered TUI output,
# which always emits LF. Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true and
# actions/checkout does not override it, so without this every one of the 177
# fixtures checks out as CRLF and every comparison test fails on Windows —
# with a diff that looks like a rendering change and isn't.
*.golden -text

# Keep shell scripts LF so they stay runnable from git-bash/WSL on a Windows
# checkout, where CRLF makes the shebang line fail to parse.
*.sh text eol=lf
